"h":[null,4],"hoursOpen":false,"profileId":"P0154"},"hardened":false,"anneal":[],"advice":null,"from":{},"profileIds":["P0129","P0154"],"fromId":{}},"price":null,"notes":[{"topic":"Industrial use","items":[{"id":"Q00340","text":"Industrial heat-resistant technical parts; printer and end-use qualification required. This entry remains excluded from H2C printing.","source":"XP-thermax-psu-1","at":"Industrial use","domain":"Application","type":"Selection interpretation","category":"application","conditions":"Manufacturer high-temperature grade, not H2C validation."}]},{"topic":"Good for","items":[{"id":"Q06158","text":"PSU has excellent thermal and chemical resistance, making it well suited for demanding applications in automotive, aerospace, electronics, defense, food service, industrial, plumbing, medical, semi-con applications.","source":"XP-thermax-psu-1-2","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Benefits","items":[{"id":"Q05216","text":"High Environmental Stress Crack Resistance (ESCR)","source":"XP-thermax-psu-1-2","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06149","text":"Very high thermal properties superior to Ultem 9085","source":"XP-thermax-psu-1-2","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06150","text":"Excellent hydrolytic resistance","source":"XP-thermax-psu-1-2","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06151","text":"Sterilization capable, including EtO gas, radiation, steam autoclaving, plasma, dry heat and cold sterilization","source":"XP-thermax-psu-1-2","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06152","text":"Exceptional strength and modulus, even at elevated temperatures","source":"XP-thermax-psu-1-2","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06153","text":"Outstanding impact resistance","source":"XP-thermax-psu-1-2","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06154","text":"Highly resistant to even large (10 Mrd) doses of gamma radiation","source":"XP-thermax-psu-1-2","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06155","text":"Resists most common automotive fluids including gasoline, antifreeze, transmission fluids, motor oils, power steering fluid, windshield washer fluid (ESCR, 24 hrs, 100C)","source":"XP-thermax-psu-1-2","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06156","text":"Inherently flame retardant with low smoke evolution and low smoke toxicity","source":"XP-thermax-psu-1-2","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06159","text":"PSU is an excellent alternative to ULTEM 9085.","source":"XP-thermax-psu-1-2","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06160","text":"While having a lower cost per kilogram and lower density (giving you more filament per kilogram as well), it maintains superior thermal properties.","source":"XP-thermax-psu-1-2","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06161","text":"Its higher Tg and HDT give it higher strength and stiffness at elevated temperatures.","source":"XP-thermax-psu-1-2","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Warping and shrinkage","items":[{"id":"Q06157","text":"Excellent dimensional stability with low creep sensitivity, low and uniform coefficient of thermal expansion, and highly reproducible part-to-part dimensions.","source":"XP-thermax-psu-1-2","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Moisture sensitivity","items":[{"id":"Q06162","text":"Drying Specs 120C for 4 hours","source":"XP-thermax-psu-1-2","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]}]}],"layers":[],"published":[],"environm